---
import IllustrationFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/IllustrationFigure.astro"
import SvgFigure from "~/components/illustration-kit/SvgFigure.astro"
import { series, stroke } from "~/data/palette"
---

<IllustrationFigure lead="Which treatment succeeds more often?">
  <SvgFigure
    name="simpson"
    class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm"
    viewBox="0 0 300 366"
    title="Treatment A wins in both stone-size groups, but B wins overall"
    desc="With small stones, A succeeds in 81 of 87 cases (93 percent), while B succeeds in 234 of 270 (87 percent). With large stones, A succeeds in 192 of 263 (73 percent), while B succeeds in 55 of 80 (69 percent). Combined, A succeeds in 273 of 350 (78 percent) and B in 289 of 350 (83 percent)."
  >
    <g fill="currentColor" font-family="sans-serif">
      <text x="8" y="18" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">
        Small stones
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="44" font-size="16">
        A: 81 of 87
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="50" width="223.2" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-red)" />
      <text x="237.2" y="63" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        93%
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="88" font-size="16">
        B: 234 of 270
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="94" width="208.8" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-blue)" />
      <text x="222.8" y="107" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        87%
      </text>
      <path d="M8 116 H292" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.2" />
      <text x="8" y="144" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">
        Large stones
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="170" font-size="16">
        A: 192 of 263
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="176" width="175.2" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-red)" />
      <text x="189.2" y="189" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        73%
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="214" font-size="16">
        B: 55 of 80
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="220" width="165.6" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-blue)" />
      <text x="179.6" y="233" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        69%
      </text>
      <path d="M8 242 H292" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1" stroke-opacity="0.2" />
      <text x="8" y="270" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">
        All patients
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="296" font-size="16">
        A: 273 of 350
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="302" width="187.2" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-red)" />
      <text x="201.2" y="315" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        78%
      </text>
      <text x="8" y="340" font-size="16">
        B: 289 of 350
      </text>
      <rect x="8" y="346" width="199.2" height="14" fill="var(--color-series-blue)" />
      <text x="213.2" y="359" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">
        83%
      </text>
    </g>
  </SvgFigure>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
    <p class="font-bold">Why does the overall winner change?</p>
    <p class="text-base leading-normal">
      Treatment A was used mainly for harder, large stones. Treatment B was used mainly
      for easier, small stones. The lengths below show the patient counts, not success rates.
    </p>
    <SvgFigure
      name="simpson-patient-mix"
      class="mx-auto w-full max-w-lg"
      viewBox="0 0 500 170"
      title="Different mixes of easy and hard cases for each treatment"
      desc="Both treatments saw 350 patients. Treatment A treated 87 with small stones and 263 with large stones. Treatment B treated 270 with small stones and 80 with large stones. The relative widths show the numbers of people in each category, explaining how B had a higher overall success rate despite A's higher success rates within each category."
    >
      <g fill="currentColor" font-size="17" font-weight="700">
        <text x="8" y="56">A</text>
        <text x="8" y="113">B</text>
        <text x="280" y="18" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">350 patients per treatment</text>
      </g>
      {[
        { y: 34, small: 87, large: 263 },
        { y: 91, small: 270, large: 80 },
      ].map(({ y, small, large }) => {
        const x = 58
        const w = 420
        const smallW = (w * small) / 350
        return (
          <g>
            <rect x={x} y={y} width={smallW} height="34" fill={series.green} />
            <rect x={x + smallW} y={y} width={w - smallW} height="34" fill={series.gold} />
            <rect x={x} y={y} width={w} height="34" stroke={stroke} fill="none" stroke-width="1.5" />
            <text x={x + smallW / 2} y={y + 23} text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="700"
              fill="var(--color-ink)">{small}</text>
            <text x={x + smallW + (w - smallW) / 2} y={y + 23} text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="700"
              fill="var(--color-ink)">{large}</text>
          </g>
        )
      })}
      <g font-size="15" fill="currentColor">
        <rect x="58" y="144" width="14" height="14" fill={series.green} />
        <text x="79" y="156">Small stones</text>
        <rect x="258" y="144" width="14" height="14" fill={series.gold} />
        <text x="279" y="156">Large stones</text>
      </g>
    </SvgFigure>
    <p class="text-base leading-normal">
      A treated 263 people with harder, large stones; B treated 270 with easier, small stones.
      This unequal mix makes A's overall rate look worse, even though A did better
      within each stone-size group.
    </p>
  </div>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    Bars show success rates from the kidney stone study. A wins for small stones and large
    stones separately. But A treated mostly large, harder stones (263 of 350 patients), while B
    treated mostly small stones (270 of 350). Combining the groups reverses the result.
  </Fragment>
</IllustrationFigure>
